# API & Service Hooks

## Domain layout (`src/core/api/<domain>/`)

- `*.api.ts` — public client class using `HttpClient` + `callNoError`
- `*.admin.api.ts` — admin endpoints when needed
- `*.models.ts` — request/response types
- `*.helpers.ts` — response mappers/transformers
- Wire new clients on `DansshipAPI` in `dansship.api.ts` and re-export models from `core/api/index.ts`

```ts
async getFigures(payload?: GetFiguresParams) {
  return this.httpClient.callNoError<OffsetPaginatedResponse<Figure>, object, GetFiguresResponse>(
    { path: '/figures', method: 'GET', params: payload },
    response => ({
      figures: response.data.map(transformFigure),
      total: response.total,
    }),
  );
}
```

## Service hooks (`src/hooks/services/`)

- Name: `use-<domain>.ts`; re-export from `hooks/services/index.ts` and `@hooks`
- Call `DansshipAPI.<domain>.*` via `useCallablePromise` (or existing promise helpers)
- Keep loading/pagination/filter state in the hook; pages/modules consume the returned API shape

```ts
const { isLoading, call } = useCallablePromise((payload: GetFiguresParams) =>
  DansshipAPI.figures.getFigures(payload),
);
```

Do not fetch raw envelopes in page components — normalize in API helpers / context, then expose clean domain types to UI.
